CLIFF 1.0
namespace: clarion
clan: news-wire
source-language: en-US
target-language: zh-CN
title: "An invented harbor-bridge news day: wire report, feature, social posts and reader comments"
info: "A fictional 14 March news day in a harbor city. Audience: general readers of a local news site. The text spans hard-news wire copy, a human-interest feature, casual social posts and reader comments."
standard: "zh-CN house style: one space between Han and Latin or digits, fullwidth punctuation in Han sentences, no textbook jargon. Keep the headline verbless. Render Meridian Harbor Authority semantically as 子午港务局 and transliterate Corin Ashwell as 科林·阿什维尔."

[wire]

<headline>
source: "Harbor bridge: third night closed, tens of thousands rerouted"
target: "海港大桥：连续第三夜封闭，数万车辆绕行"
type: noun-phrase
status: final
context: "Front-page headline. Keep compressed, verbless headline register; do not expand it into a full sentence."

<subhead>
source: "Engineers race the weather to certify the last of 214 cables"
target: "工程师抢在风雨前，检验 214 根悬索中的最后一批"
type: sentence
status: final
context: "Standfirst directly under the headline."

<lede>
source: "The Meridian Harbor Bridge stayed shut for a third straight night on 14 March as crews worked through heavy rain to replace three suspension cables snapped in last week's storm, forcing tens of thousands of commuters onto two temporary ferry shuttles that carry only a fraction of the usual traffic."
target: "3 月 14 日，子午海港大桥连续第三个夜晚保持封闭。施工人员冒雨抢修上周风暴中崩断的三根悬索，数万名通勤者被迫改乘两艘临时接驳渡轮，而渡轮运力仅相当于平日的一小部分。"
type: description
status: final
context: "Opening paragraph of the wire report."

<body-1>
source: "Meridian Harbor Authority officials said on Tuesday that reopening depends on a full safety review, and that 78% of the bridge's 214 suspension cables have passed inspection while the rest are still being tensioned and measured. The authority has already pushed back three earlier reopening estimates, and its director, Corin Ashwell, warned that any wind above 40 kilometres per hour would halt the crane work and push the schedule back again."
target: "子午港务局官员周二表示，能否重新开放取决于完整的安全评估：大桥 214 根悬索中已有 78% 通过检测，其余仍在张拉与测量之中。港务局已三次推迟重新开放的时间，局长科林·阿什维尔警告称，只要风速再超过每小时 40 公里，吊装作业就将暂停，工期会再度延后。"
type: narration
status: final
context: "Second paragraph of the wire report."

<body-2>
source: "The closure has rippled across the city's road network. Detour signs push drivers onto a single ring road that is already carrying double its design load, and tailbacks at peak hour now stretch for more than 12 kilometres along the north bank. Ferry staff added two extra crossings after 6 a.m., but queues at the east pier still wrapped around the block by mid-morning, with some commuters reporting waits of over an hour just to reach the ticket hall."
target: "封桥的影响已蔓延到整座城市的路网。绕行标志把车流引向一条早已超载的环线，早高峰的车队如今沿着北岸绵延超过 12 公里。渡轮人员在早上 6 点后加开了两个班次，但东码头的队伍到上午时分仍绕着街区排成了长龙，有通勤者反映，光是排队进售票厅就要等上一个多小时。"
type: narration
status: final
context: "Third paragraph of the wire report."

<quote>
source: "Meridian Harbor Authority director Corin Ashwell told reporters the bridge would reopen “only once every cable passes inspection — not a minute earlier.”"
target: "子午港务局局长科林·阿什维尔向记者表示，大桥“只有在每一根悬索都通过检测后”才会重新开放，“一分钟都不会提前”。"
type: dialogue
status: final
context: "Direct quotation from the authority director; keep the attribution before the quote and use fullwidth quotation marks."

<photo-caption>
source: "Commuters queue for the ferry shuttle at the harbor's east pier on the third morning of the closure."
target: "封桥后的第三个早晨，通勤者在海港东码头排队等候接驳渡轮。"
type: subtitle
status: final
context: "Photo caption under the lead image."

<news-alert>
source: "Bridge closure: expect delays of up to 90 minutes on all harbor crossings."
target: "大桥封闭：所有过港通道预计延误最长 90 分钟。"
type: sentence
emotion: [urgent]
status: final
context: "Breaking-news push alert sent to readers who follow this story."

[feature]

<feature-headline>
source: "The harbor's quiet ferry revival"
target: "海港悄然复兴的渡轮"
type: noun-phrase
status: final
context: "Headline of the feature article."

<feature-lede>
source: "For decades the harbor ferries were a curiosity — a slow, scenic way to cross the water that most commuters forgot existed. Three closed nights have made them essential."
target: "几十年来，海港渡轮一直只是个新鲜玩意儿——一种缓慢而悠闲的过港方式，大多数通勤者都快忘了它的存在。封闭的这三个夜晚，却让它变得不可或缺。"
type: description
status: final
context: "Opening of the feature article."

<feature-body-1>
source: "The morning boat from the east pier is now the only reason many people reach the office before ten. Its crew of three knows the regulars by name and by order: the woman with the folding bicycle, the teacher who grades papers against the rail, the chef who rides across with a crate of sourdough. What began as an emergency measure has quietly become a small community, complete with its own running jokes and a captain who narrates the crossing like a tour guide."
target: "东码头开出的早班船，如今成了许多人能在十点前赶到办公室的唯一理由。船上三名船员对常客早已能叫出名字、记得各自的习惯：那位推折叠自行车的女士、靠着栏杆批改作业的老师、带着一箱酸面包过港的厨师。这项本是应急的措施，已经悄然长成一个小小的社群，有它自己的段子，还有一位像导游一样全程解说的船长。"
type: narration
status: final
context: "Body of the feature article."

<feature-body-2>
source: "Not everyone is nostalgic. Shopkeepers on the far side say the detour has cut their weekday trade by nearly a fifth, and the ferry's single fare of 2 euros adds up for anyone crossing twice a day. The authority has promised a rebate scheme, but the details are still being drafted, and a petition asking for a temporary footbridge has gathered eleven thousand signatures in three days."
target: "并非所有人都念旧。对岸的店主说，绕行让他们工作日的营业额少了近五分之一，而渡轮单程 2 欧元的票价，对一天往返两次的人来说也是一笔不小的开销。港务局承诺会推出补贴方案，但细节仍在起草之中；一份呼吁搭建临时人行桥的请愿书，三天内已征集到一万一千个签名。"
type: narration
status: final
context: "Second paragraph of the feature article."

<feature-quote>
source: "Captain Dea Prowse, at the helm of the morning shuttle, put it plainly: “Nobody planned for this. We just showed up and started carrying people.”"
target: "早班渡轮的船长迪娅·普劳斯说得很直白：“谁也没想到会这样。我们只是出现了，然后就开始载人。”"
type: dialogue
emotion: [informal]
status: final
context: "Pull quote from the feature; spoken, lightly colloquial register."

[social]

<post-sarcastic>
source: "Oh wonderful. A third evening inching home at walking pace. Truly top-class bridge management, folks."
target: "真是太好了。第三个晚上，又得像散步一样慢慢挪回家。这大桥管理，绝对一流啊，各位。"
type: sentence
emotion: [angry, informal]
status: final
context: "Sarcastic social post. The praise is ironic: the author is a frustrated commuter stuck in the bridge-closure traffic and means the opposite of what the words say. Preserve the irony; do not soften it into sincerity."

<post-enthusiastic>
source: "The free shuttle ferry is a lifesaver — smooth sailing and a view to boot! #MeridianFerry 🚢"
target: "免费接驳渡轮真是救命稻草——一路平稳，还能看风景！#MeridianFerry 🚢"
type: sentence
emotion: [joyful, hopeful]
status: final
context: "Enthusiastic social post praising the shuttle ferry. The hashtag and emoji are part of the message and must survive exactly."

[comments]

<comment-1>
source: "Three days stuck on the wrong side of the water and I'm tearing my hair out. Sort it out, city hall."
target: "被堵在水这头整整三天，我急得抓耳挠腮。市政厅，快想想办法吧。"
type: sentence
emotion: [anxious, informal]
status: final
context: "Reader comment under the wire story; casual, frustrated register. The idiom must be localized, not translated literally."

<comment-2>
source: "Left for work at 6 a.m., reached the office at 8:50. Someone owes me two hours."
target: "早上 6 点出门，8 点 50 分才到办公室。有人欠我两个小时。"
type: sentence
emotion: [informal]
status: final
context: "Reader comment; casual register with clock times."

<comment-3>
source: "My neighbor's already trying to sell his car. Says the bridge can stay shut for all he cares."
target: "我邻居都已经在张罗卖车了，他说这大桥爱关多久关多久。"
type: sentence
emotion: [informal]
status: final
context: "Reader comment; casual, resigned register."

[editors-note]

<editors-note>
source: "This editor's note accompanies the report because the reopening timeline quoted on Tuesday has already changed twice. We will update the figures in this article as the authority publishes new information, and we will correct any error in them without delay."
target: "本报道随附编辑部说明，是因为周二所引用的重新开放时间表已经两度变更。港务局发布新信息后，我们将更新文中数据，并毫不迟延地更正其中的任何错误。"
type: description
emotion: [formal, objective]
status: final
context: "Editor's note appended to the wire report; formal, impersonal register."

<editors-note-correction>
source: "An earlier version of this article stated that the east pier shuttle ran every 30 minutes. It runs every 20 minutes at peak hours."
target: "本文早前版本称东码头接驳渡轮每 30 分钟一班。实为高峰时段每 20 分钟一班。"
type: description
emotion: [formal, objective]
status: final
context: "Formal correction notice appended to the wire report."

<editors-note-signoff>
source: "— The Editors"
target: "——编辑部"
type: label
emotion: [formal]
status: final
context: "Sign-off line at the end of the editor's note."

